Id: lin032w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set net.ipv4.conf.all.send_redirects=0 and .default.send_redirects=0 in /etc/sysctl.d.
References: sysctl.d(5); Linux kernel ip-sysctl documentation
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

net.ipv4.conf.*.send_redirects is 1, so this host sends ICMP redirects.
Only a router has reason to; from a host they can be used to steer
other machines' traffic:
  # sysctl -w net.ipv4.conf.all.send_redirects=0
  # sysctl -w net.ipv4.conf.default.send_redirects=0
